== Chapter XV

#align(center)[#block(width: 85%)[
  #set par(justify: false)
  #strong[Concerning God’s purpose.]
]]

#v(0.9em)

3\. #smallcaps[The] third and last thing in the text, which I will only glance at briefly, is the ground and origin of our #emph[effectual calling,] in these words: κατὰ πρόθεσιν, “according to His purpose.” #emph[Anselm] renders it #emph[according to his good will]#footnote[#emph[Signif. aeternum Dei beneplacitum.] \[It signifies the eternal good pleasure of God.\] Anselm.]. #emph[Peter Martyr] reads it κατὰ γνώμην, according to his #emph[decree,] and #emph[Beza] interprets it the same way. This purpose, or decree, of God is the fountainhead of all our spiritual blessings#footnote[πρόθεσις #emph[est decretum Dei, ab aeterno sanctum, ex mera ipsius non scrutanda sed adoranda voluntate.] \[Πρόθεσις is the decree of God, ordained from eternity out of his mere will, which is not to be searched into but adored.\] Beza]. It is the #emph[causa] προηγουμένη, the impulsive, or moving, cause of our calling, justification, and glorification. It is the highest link in the golden chain of salvation. Why is one man called and not another? It is from the eternal purpose of God. God’s decree gives the casting vote in man’s salvation.
